#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:861
msgid ""
"Most of the parameters in this list have numerical values. Some have string "
"values, that point to particular python functions within PyBaMM. These "
"denote parameters that vary over time and/or space, in a manner defined by "
"the given python function. For the moment we will ignore these, and focus on "
"altering one of the numerical parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:863
msgid ""
"The class ```pybamm.ParameterValues`` <https://docs.pybamm.org/en/latest/"
"source/api/parameters/parameter_values.html>`__ acts like the normal python "
"``dict`` data structure, so you can read or write individual parameters "
"accordingly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:-1
msgid "[5]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"variable = \"Current function [A]\"\n"
"old_value = param[variable]\n"
"param[variable] = 1.4\n"
"new_value = param[variable]\n"
"print(variable, \"was\", old_value)\n"
"print(variable, \"now is\", param[variable])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:889
msgid ""
"<pre>\n"
"Current function [A] was 0.680616\n"
"Current function [A] now is 1.4\n"
"</pre>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:896
msgid ""
"\\begin{sphinxVerbatim}[commandchars=\\\\\\{\\}]\n"
"Current function [A] was 0.680616\n"
"Current function [A] now is 1.4\n"
"\\end{sphinxVerbatim}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:904
msgid ""
"Current function [A] was 0.680616\n"
"Current function [A] now is 1.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:916
msgid ""
"In order to compare solutions with different parameter values, parameters "
"must be changed to ``InputParameter`` objects, whose value can then be "
"specified when solving. For example, we can compare the Voltage calculated "
"using both the old and new current values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:-1
msgid "[6]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# Set up\n"
"model = pybamm.lithium_ion.SPM()\n"
"solver = model.default_solver\n"
"param[\"Current function [A]\"] = \"[input]\"\n"
"param.process_model(model)\n"
"disc.process_model(model)\n"
"\n"
"# Solution with current = 0.68\n"
"old_solution = solver.solve(model, t_eval, inputs={\"Current function [A]\": "
"0.68})\n"
"old_time = old_solution[\"Time [h]\"].entries\n"
"old_voltage = old_solution[\"Voltage [V]\"].entries\n"
"\n"
"# Solution with current = 1.4\n"
"new_solution = solver.solve(model, t_eval, inputs={\"Current function [A]\": "
"1.4})\n"
"new_time = new_solution[\"Time [h]\"].entries\n"
"new_voltage = new_solution[\"Voltage [V]\"].entries\n"
"\n"
"plt.plot(old_time, old_voltage, lw=2, label=\"Current = 0.68\")\n"
"plt.plot(new_time, new_voltage, lw=2, label=\"Current = 1.4\")\n"
"plt.xlabel(\"Time [h]\", fontsize=15)\n"
"plt.ylabel(\"Voltage [V]\", fontsize=15)\n"
"plt.legend(fontsize=15)\n"
"plt.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:967
msgid ""
"Note that there is a small number of parameters for which this is not "
"possible, since the discretisation depends on them (for example, *Negative "
"electrode thickness*). In this case you would need to remesh the geometry as "
"the relative length of the electrodes would have altered. This would in turn "
"require you to re-discretise the model equations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/change-settings.ipynb:981
